From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0100
Subject: drm/cix: dptx: clear the ELD when the EDID read fails

When the EDID read fails, get_modes keeps the ELD of the previous sink.
get_eld then reports audio formats that the new sink may not support.
Clear the EDID property, which also clears the ELD.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/cix/dptx/trilin_drm.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/cix/dptx/trilin_drm.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/cix/dptx/trilin_drm.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/cix/dptx/trilin_drm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/cix/dptx/trilin_drm.c
@@ -362,6 +362,11 @@ static int trilin_dp_connector_get_modes(struct drm_connector *connector)
 		}
 
 		if (!edid) {
+			/* Drop the ELD of the previous sink, and tell hdmi-codec. */
+			drm_connector_update_edid_property(connector, NULL);
+			dptx_audio_handle_plugged_change(&dp->dp_audio,
+							 trilin_dp_plugged_status(dp));
+
 			mode = drm_dp_downstream_mode(connector->dev, dp->dpcd,
 						      dp->downstream_ports);
 			if (mode) {
-- 
